From: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0031] cmake: probe and enable AVX2 and FMA runtime vectorization

Probe compiler support for -mavx2 and -mfma flags on Clang/GNU, exporting
them to ps3recomp_runtime when supported. This enables the hardware AVX2
and FMA fast paths in spu_helpers.h across all lifted SPU jobs and runtime
SIMD helpers.

---
 CMakeLists.txt | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index a39405d6..0bd4ca54 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -363,6 +363,14 @@ if(CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "Clang|GNU")
         # the runtime's existing ISA requirement so their fast path agrees.
         target_compile_options(ps3recomp_runtime PUBLIC -msse4.1)
     endif()
+    check_c_compiler_flag(-mavx2 PS3RECOMP_HAS_MAVX2)
+    if(PS3RECOMP_HAS_MAVX2)
+        target_compile_options(ps3recomp_runtime PUBLIC -mavx2)
+    endif()
+    check_c_compiler_flag(-mfma PS3RECOMP_HAS_MFMA)
+    if(PS3RECOMP_HAS_MFMA)
+        target_compile_options(ps3recomp_runtime PUBLIC -mfma)
+    endif()
 elseif(MSVC)
     # Real cl.exe -- clang-cl reports its id as Clang and is handled above.
     #
-- 
2.43.0
